This README file contains information on the contents of the meta-bao layer.

Please see the corresponding sections below for details.

Dependencies
============

  URI: meta-toradex-torizon
  branch: 5d4df8065d2989d84bd120f0a1e2a6ab0567ab07

Patches
=======

Please submit any patches against the meta-bao layer by opening a pull request
at https://github.com/bao-project/meta-bao

Maintainer: David Cerdeira <davidmcerdeira@gmail.com>

Table of Contents
=================

  I. Adding the meta-bao layer to your build
 II. Misc


I. Adding the meta-bao layer to your build
=================================================

Run 'bitbake-layers add-layer meta-bao'

II. Misc
========

meta-bao is a Yocto/OpenEmbedded layer that provides Linux kernel patches and
configuration to run TorizonOS as a guest under the Bao hypervisor alongside a
FreeRTOS guest. It targets the Toradex Verdin iMX8MP and is compatible with
the Yocto scarthgap release.

The layer appends the linux-toradex 6.6-2.1.x recipe with the following:

  - 0001-add-bao-ipcshmem-driver.patch
      Adds the Bao IPC shared memory driver (drivers/bao/bao-ipcshmem.c)
      to the kernel source tree.

  - 0002-Remove-imx8mp-UART3-and-CPU3.patch
      Removes UART3 and CPU3 from imx8mp device trees, freeing those
      resources for exclusive use by the FreeRTOS guest.

  - 0003-Add-bao-device-tree-node.patch
      Adds the bao-ipc@f0000000 shared memory node to imx8mp-verdin.dtsi,
      describing the IPC region used for inter-VM communication.

  - enablebaodriver.cfg
      Kernel config fragment that enables CONFIG_BAO_SHMEM=y.
